667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The shift register, which allows serial input \(one bit after the other through a single data line\) and produces a parallel output is known as the Serial-In Parallel-Out shift register. The logic circuit given below shows a serial-in-parallel-out shift register. The circuit consists of four D flip-flops which are connected. The clear \(CLR\) signal is connected in addition to the clock signal to all 4 flip flops in order to RESET them. The output of the first flip-flop is connected to the input of the next flip flop and so on. All these flip-flops are synchronous with each other since the same clock signal is applied to each flip-flop. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
